      "message": "test(motion): pin the straight link at the holes, not at the rim row\n\nThe finish3d_gaplink pin asserted no traverse at the retract plane\non the holed plate. The straight author erases every hop over the\ntwo holes, but the rows off the plate's outside rim keep theirs:\nthere the march itself rests the ball about 0.005 mm into the outer\nflank inside exact tangency (its own chord budget), and the exact\nsweep verdict refuses a link whose ends bite the flank. The refusal\nis the law: certified or not at all (gaplink.rs).\n\n- straight_links_holes_at_the_run_height now asserts no rapid at\n  the retract height crosses a hole centre line, and that the\n  rim-to-rim feed links stand.\n- jump_mode_still_hops_over_the_holes: the negative control. The\n  plain author hops both holes on the same fixture, so the pin\n  proves the author, not a fixture without holes to cross.\n\nRefs #1708",
